WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.043
Meet Priya.

2
00:00:02.393 --> 00:00:06.083
She runs finance operations
at a fast-growing company,

3
00:00:06.123 --> 00:00:09.173
where AI agents now work
alongside her team,

4
00:00:09.213 --> 00:00:12.947
issuing refunds, updating
records and approving payments.

5
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.964
The agents are fast.

6
00:00:15.264 --> 00:00:17.735
But they act on whatever
access they were given.

7
00:00:18.034 --> 00:00:20.972
Nobody checks first,
and nothing records why.

8
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:25.573
Then, one Friday night,
an agent misreads a request,

9
00:00:25.613 --> 00:00:27.929
and refunds 900,000 dirhams.

10
00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:31.272
Another exports 38,000 customer records.

11
00:00:31.822 --> 00:00:34.728
On Monday, the auditors ask:
who approved this?

12
00:00:35.128 --> 00:00:36.336
Nobody did.

13
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.540
That's why we built AgentPermit:

14
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.641
a checkpoint between your
AI agents and your systems.

15
00:00:44.041 --> 00:00:46.474
Every agent, explicitly permitted.

16
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:50.295
Before an agent acts,
it asks AgentPermit first.

17
00:00:50.595 --> 00:00:54.926
Its identity comes from its sign-in,
so it can't pretend to be anyone else.

18
00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:56.920
Then your rules decide.

19
00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.985
Routine actions go straight through,
risky ones are stopped,

20
00:01:01.025 --> 00:01:03.784
and anything in between
waits for a named person.

21
00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:08.278
So when an agent tries to
refund 900,000 dirhams,

22
00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:11.253
Priya gets the request on
her phone, and rejects it.

23
00:01:11.653 --> 00:01:12.865
Nothing runs.

24
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.597
There's no way around the checkpoint.

25
00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:18.097
And every decision leaves a signed,

26
00:01:18.137 --> 00:01:21.478
chained receipt that auditors
can verify on their own.

27
00:01:22.383 --> 00:01:25.043
AgentPermit runs in your own Azure tenant,

28
00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:28.188
and works with Copilot Studio,
Power Platform,

29
00:01:28.228 --> 00:01:33.313
Microsoft Teams, any agent
through its REST API, and MCP.

30
00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:36.072
Use it wherever agents move money,

31
00:01:36.112 --> 00:01:38.832
change access or touch sensitive data:

32
00:01:38.872 --> 00:01:43.410
in finance, banking, HR, IT,
healthcare and procurement.

33
00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.220
AgentPermit, from Plinthera.

34
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.703
Every agent, explicitly permitted.

35
00:01:50.052 --> 00:01:51.336
Book your demo today.
